node_modules/
dist/
.DS_Store
*.log

# The colosseum (arena spectator app) is a separate Cloudflare/nsite deliverable,
# not part of the game server — its deploy copy lives here for convenience only.
arena/

# Working notes that live in the repo root but are NOT the repo's: audit output
# and investigation write-ups. They have sat untracked and unignored for weeks,
# which means one `git add -A` publishes them to a public repo. Ignored so that
# cannot happen by accident.
findings-merged.md
lag-report.md
flavor-audit.md
events-scope.md
mob-audit.md
mob-weirdness.md

# THE ROOM PLATES STAY OUT. Generated art, megabytes of it, and the set only
# grows — there is no reason for a public repo to carry it and every reason not
# to bloat its history with binaries that will be regenerated anyway. Nothing
# breaks without them: a terrain with no plate paints bare ground, which is the
# behaviour the client was built around from the first day. They are uploaded
# from the working tree at deploy time, so KEEP A COPY — a fresh clone can
# deploy the game correctly but will deploy it without pictures.
game-server/public/room-bg/
# THE STAGED PREVIEW BUILDS. Both are generated from src/public.ts by
# build-mob-preview.mjs and neither is a source of anything: preview/ is the
# working page and its three folders are symlinks into public/, and nsite/ is a
# trimmed COPY cut for publishing, which means committing it would put a second
# copy of 35MB of art in the repo. Rebuild either in one command.
game-server/preview/
game-server/nsite/
# ...and the creature sprites, for the same reasons and at the same cost:
# they upload from the working tree at deploy, so KEEP A COPY.
game-server/public/mob/
# ...and the nine skies. These are the ones it would hurt most to lose, because
# unlike a plate they are not per-room: every layered scene in the world is
# painted with its sky cut out and one of these drawn behind it, so without them
# the whole set has a hole where the weather goes. KEEP A COPY.
game-server/public/sky/

# THE WORKBENCH. Generated art in progress — frame sets, per-creature working
# directories, the image-gen scratch — 88MB of it and growing every session. Same
# reasoning as the room plates above: binaries that get regenerated, in a repo
# that has no use for their history. Nothing breaks without them; they are not
# inputs to the game, they are what the finished sprites were cut FROM.
output/
# ...and this machine's own Claude Code permission list. It is local by
# definition (that is what the .local suffix means), and it carries absolute
# paths under the home directory — which on this repo is a dox risk and not a
# hypothetical one. The shared .claude/settings.json, if there ever is one, is
# deliberately NOT ignored: config meant for everybody should be visible.
.claude/settings.local.json
# The mob preview page and its symlink to the art (scripts/build-mob-preview.mjs).
game-server/preview/

# ---- THE RAW SPRITE SHEETS (2026-09-09). 18MB of generator output that nothing
# in the game reads: they are the INPUT to the strip pipeline, not part of it.
# The route is generator sheet -> scripts/normalize_*.py (grid and fragment
# clean-up) -> game-server/scripts/cut-mob-sheet.mjs (pose PNGs) ->
# build-mob-strips.mjs (the .webp the client loads). Only the last of those is
# in public/mob/, which is itself ignored and kept in the working tree.
#
# KEEP A COPY, same bargain as the plates: nine of the sixteen have a finished
# strip and seven do not, so this is also unfinished work, and re-generating a
# sheet does not reproduce the one that was cut.
assets/sprites/
